{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"enharmonic-cummy-olm","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`clarity_check` can return `verdict: \"fail\"` while its own reported evidence says the ticket\npassed, and its MCP output carries no field that explains why. A caller sees\n`score >= threshold` next to `verdict: fail` and has nothing to act on.\n\nObserved 2026-08-27 against the LIVE MCP server, on probe ticket\n`ruby-griffinish-goitered` (`c67b-ece5-707e-460e`):\n\n```\nclarity_check {\"ticket_id\": \"ruby-griffinish-goitered\"}\n  -> {\"score\": 6, \"verdict\": \"fail\", \"threshold\": 5, \"passed\": false}\n```\n\n6 >= 5, yet `fail`. The description at that moment had an `## Acceptance Criteria` section\nwhose items were plain `- AC1: ...` bullets rather than `- [ ]` checkboxes. After rewriting\nthe same ticket's ACs as checkboxes, the identical call returned\n`{\"score\": 7, \"verdict\": \"pass\", \"threshold\": 5, \"passed\": true}` — confirming the failure came\nfrom the structural floor, not the score.\n\n## Mechanism\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py:165-169`\n\n```python\nscore = _clarity_score(description, ticket_type)\nfloor = evaluate_plan_clarity(description)\nif score >= threshold and floor.passes:\n    return {\"score\": score, \"verdict\": \"pass\", \"threshold\": threshold}, 0\nreturn {\"score\": score, \"verdict\": \"fail\", \"threshold\": threshold}, 1\n```\n\nThe verdict is a conjunction of two independent conditions, but only the score half is\nreturned. `PlanClarityFloor` (`src/rebar/_plan_clarity.py:44-56`) already carries the exact\nevidence — `ac_items`, `empty_ac_items`, `sentinel_assignments`, `unchecked_ac_lines` — and all\nof it is discarded here.\n\nThe MCP output model has no place to put it either:\n`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:162-166`\n\n```python\nclass ClarityResultOut(_Out):\n    score: int\n    verdict: str\n    threshold: int\n    passed: bool | None = None\n```\n\nNote the library's own read-error branch (`src/rebar/_lib_gates.py:49-52`) DOES return a\n`reason`, so the field exists on the failure path that cannot happen in normal use and is\nmissing on the one that can.\n\n## Impact\n`clarity_check` is a read-only gate tool agents use to decide whether a plan is dispatchable.\nOn the common failure (bulleted instead of checkbox ACs, or a `TBD`/`TODO` sentinel in a value\nposition) it returns a self-contradictory result with no remediation signal, so the caller must\nguess or re-derive the floor. The related `check_ac` returns a `reason` string in exactly this\nsituation, so the two sibling gates are inconsistent.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Create a ticket whose description scores at or above the clarity threshold but whose\n   `## Acceptance Criteria` items are plain `-` bullets, not `- [ ]` checkboxes.\n2. Call `clarity_check` on it.\n3. Observe `verdict: \"fail\"` with `score >= threshold` and no explanatory field.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1: `clarity_check_compute` returns a `reason` naming which condition failed — the score floor, or the structural floor — and, for the structural floor, which defect (missing checklist, empty AC item, or unresolved sentinel with its line).\n- [ ] AC2: `ClarityResultOut` carries that `reason` so it survives to MCP callers.\n- [ ] AC3: A pass still returns `verdict: \"pass\"` with the existing shape; the added field is additive and does not break existing consumers.\n- [ ] AC4: A regression test asserts that a description with `score >= threshold` and non-checkbox ACs yields `verdict: \"fail\"` with a non-empty `reason` naming the structural floor.\n- [ ] AC5: A regression test asserts a below-threshold description yields a `reason` naming the score.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- [ ] DD1: AC1-AC3 implemented; AC4 and AC5 tests pass.\n- [ ] DD2: `docs/mcp-reference.md` regenerated if the tool summary changes.\n","id":"34a5-4905-d75f-4886","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["mcp","gates"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"clarity_check returns verdict=fail with score >= threshold and no reason, hiding the structural-floor cause"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787815191022235910,"uuid":"8492151b-703e-44e1-9408-497222436e11"}